--TEST--
the first entry of a filter, whose callback can throw an error but writes nothing, warns W1034 on the written form and names `Core\Arr::find`, `rule:ide/a-quick-fix-is-a-diagnostics-own-suggestion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Shop {
    public static function firstLarge(array<int> $prices): int {
        // `$price * 2` can overflow, so this callback can throw an error.
        return Core\Arr::first(Core\Arr::filter($prices, fn(int $price): bool => $price * 2 > 10)) ?? 0;
    }
}
--REQUEST--
diagnostics
--EXPECT--
2:13-2:17 hint - a class `Shop` is not used anywhere in this workspace
3:28-3:38 hint - a method `Shop::firstLarge` is not used anywhere in this workspace
5:16-5:99 warning W1034 `Core\Arr::find` gives the same result faster
